.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		The energy of two hydrogen atoms as they approach, from 5.0 to 0.4 Å apart. This calculation shows how a chemical bond forms: the minimum of the curve is the bond length and its depth below the separated atoms is the bond energy.
